hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15509","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym informed me that Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed him that his father al-Aswad saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taking the pledge from the people on the day of the Conquest, he said: He sat at Qarn Masqalah and took the pledge from the people upon Islam and the Shahadah, he said: I said: And what is the Shahadah? He said: Muhammad ibn al-Aswad ibn Khalaf informed me that he took their pledge upon belief in Allah and testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
